# C++ Port Scanner Makefile learning placeholder
#
# This file intentionally contains comments only. No target, variable assignment,
# dependency rule, or recipe has been implemented for you.
#
# Session 11 in ../CPP_LEARNING_PLAN.md is where you will write the build rules.
# Before then, use the comments below as a checklist and keep this file inert.
#
# Planned toolchain:
#   - C++20 compiler selected by the learner (for example, g++)
#   - include search path rooted at include/
#   - debug symbols in the development build
#   - warnings enabled so diagnostics become part of the learning workflow
#
# Planned build concepts to implement:
#   - A variable for the compiler.
#   - A variable for compiler flags.
#   - A variable for the public include directory.
#   - A source list containing src/main.cpp and the module .cpp files.
#   - A normal executable target named port_scanner.
#   - A debug target or debug configuration.
#   - A clean target that removes generated build output only.
#   - An explicit default target and appropriate phony declarations.
#
# Build design notes:
#   - Compile and link as separate concepts even if the first rule combines them.
#   - Keep generated objects and the executable under a build/ directory.
#   - Make each object depend on its source and the headers it includes.
#   - Quote or avoid shell-sensitive paths; the project is expected under Linux/WSL.
#   - Use tab-indented recipe lines when recipes are eventually added.
#   - Do not use this project to run a network scan automatically from a build rule.
#
# Learning checkpoints:
#   1. Explain how a compiler turns one translation unit into an object file.
#   2. Explain how the linker resolves declarations to definitions.
#   3. Compare a compile error with an undefined-reference link error.
#   4. Rebuild after changing one header and observe which objects need rebuilding.
#   5. Confirm clean removes generated artifacts without deleting source or notes.
#
# The final build command and supported compiler version should be documented in
# ../README.md after the build lesson.